{#
compose/_sent_optimistic.stream.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Send, answered optimistically: the composer closes now, the mail is where it
will live, and the cancel moves to a toast that counts down beside it.

The other half of a user setting — see User::SETTING_COMPOSE_SEND_FEEDBACK and
compose/_sending.stream.html.twig, which is what "hold" renders instead. The
trade is real in both directions. Holding keeps the cancel under the pointer
that just clicked: nothing moves, and the way back is exactly where the way
forward was. This gives the screen back at once and asks the user to look
somewhere else for the undo. Eight seconds of a window that will not close is a
long time when you have finished writing, and that is the complaint this
answers.

It is the DEFAULT of the two, because the wait is what people notice and the
undo is what they rarely need.

Nothing new happens here. The tidying is exactly what the end of the cancel
window does — same template, so a send cannot settle differently depending on
which shape rendered it — with its toast suppressed, because the news here is
not "sent" but "sending, and you can still stop it".

Variables: message, thread (MessageThread|null), ctx, undoUrl, cancelWindow
#}
{% include 'compose/_sent.stream.html.twig' with {
    message: message,
    thread:  thread,
    ctx:     ctx,
} only %}

{# The cancel, now that the pill is gone.
   `hide_after` IS the cancel window rather than a toast duration somebody
   picked: the Undo button goes when the toast goes, so a toast that outlived
   the window would offer a cancel that silently fails, and one that died
   early would take away a cancel that still worked. #}
<turbo-stream action="append" target="toast-region">
    <template>
        {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
            type:    'success',
            message: 'compose.sending'|trans,
            extra:   {
                undo_url:   undoUrl,
                hide_after: cancelWindow,
            },
        } only %}
    </template>
</turbo-stream>
